      "template": "bestseller_reviews",
      "body": "Hi {{name}},\n\nOne of the best parts of being an author is hearing from readers. Every message, every review, every five-star rating reminds me why I do this.\n\nHere's what people are saying about the No Blue Sky series and Tomorrow is Still Open:\n\n⭐ \"Ignition grabbed me from the first page and didn't let go. Bob Mills writes with the kind of urgency that makes you forget to eat dinner.\" — Amazon Review\n\n⭐ \"I bought No Blue Sky: Ascent for my son and ended up reading the whole thing myself before he got it back. Now we're both hooked.\" — Sarah M., Book Club Coordinator\n\n⭐ \"Tomorrow is Still Open made me cry in the best way. It's one of those books you finish and then immediately text your best friend about.\" — Goodreads Review\n\n⭐ \"The world-building in this series is incredible. Each volume gets better. Horizon (#4) had me pacing my living room during the climax.\" — David L., Sci-Fi Book Club\n\n🏆 The No Blue Sky series has been featured in Indie Sci-Fi Monthly's \"Best of the Year\" roundup and continues to gather momentum among genre fans.\n\nBut don't just take their word for it. The best way to know if these books are for you is to try one yourself.\n\nEvery volume is available as a standalone read — you can jump in anywhere, though most readers start with Ignition and work their way forward.\n\n📖 Start reading today:\n• No Blue Sky: Ignition — $9.99\n• No Blue Sky: Ascent — $11.99\n• No Blue Sky: Orbit — $12.99\n• No Blue Sky: Horizon — $14.99\n• No Blue Sky: Beyond — $14.99\n• Tomorrow is Still Open — $19.99\n\nReply anytime with questions — I'm here to help,\nBob Mills\n\nP.S. — Next week I'll be sending a special limited-time offer your way. If you've been thinking about picking up a copy, that's the week to do it.",
